---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Studio from '../components/Studio';
import { LIMITS, MODELS } from '../config';

const maxMb = LIMITS.maxInputBytes / 1024 / 1024;
---

<Base
  title="Matte: remove a video background in your browser"
  description="Remove or replace the background of a short video. Processing happens on your device; nothing is uploaded."
>
  <div class="page">
    <header class="masthead">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="Matte, home">
        <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 32 32" width="26" height="26">
          <rect width="32" height="32" rx="7" fill="currentColor"></rect>
          <path d="M16 0h9a7 7 0 0 1 7 7v18a7 7 0 0 1-7 7h-9z" fill="var(--key)"></path>
          <circle cx="16" cy="13" r="5.5" fill="var(--paper)"></circle>
          <path d="M6 29c1.6-5.6 5.4-8.3 10-8.3s8.4 2.7 10 8.3z" fill="var(--paper)"></path>
        </svg>
        Matte
      </a>
      <p class="masthead-note">No account. Nothing uploaded.</p>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="intro" aria-labelledby="intro-title">
        <h1 id="intro-title">Remove the background from a video, right on your device.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Your video is processed on your device. AI model files are downloaded when needed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <Studio client:only="react">
        <div slot="fallback" class="studio-fallback">
          <p>Loading the editor…</p>
          <noscript>This tool needs JavaScript turned on, because the video is processed by your browser.</noscript>
        </div>
      </Studio>

      <div class="notes">
        <section class="note" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
          <h2 id="privacy-title">What happens to your video</h2>
          <div class="note-body">
            <p>
              Your browser reads the file, removes the background frame by frame and writes a new video file. The video and
              its sound never leave your device: there is no upload, no server-side processing and no paid AI service.
            </p>
            <p>
              The only downloads are the AI model files, fetched from GitHub or Hugging Face the first time you use a model.
              Your browser keeps a copy, so later visits start faster. No accounts, ads, analytics or tracking.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="note" aria-labelledby="models-title">
          <h2 id="models-title">Which model should I pick?</h2>
          <div class="note-body">
            <p>
              <strong>{MODELS.rvm.name}</strong> is built for videos of people. It looks at previous frames, which helps
              keep hair and edges steady as someone moves. The download is small ({MODELS.rvm.approxDownload}).
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>{MODELS.withoutbg.name}</strong> also handles animals and objects. It looks at every frame on its own,
              so edges can flicker a little more than with People, and it needs the largest download
              ({MODELS.withoutbg.approxDownload}). On our test computer it took about 4 to 5 seconds per frame.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>{MODELS.ben2.name}</strong> keeps crisper hair and fur edges but is much slower: about 30 seconds or
              more per frame on our test computer ({MODELS.ben2.approxDownload} download). For both general models, try a
              lower frame rate and a short clip first.
            </p>
            <p>
              Neither model is perfect. Busy backgrounds, motion blur and subjects that match the background can leave
              rough edges. Use Preview this frame to check before processing the whole video.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="note" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
          <h2 id="limits-title">Current limits</h2>
          <div class="note-body">
            <ul>
              <li>Videos up to {LIMITS.maxDurationSeconds} seconds and {maxMb} MB.</li>
              <li>
                The result fits within {LIMITS.maxOutputDimension} × {LIMITS.maxOutputDimension} pixels, keeps the original
                shape and is never enlarged.
              </li>
              <li>
                Works best in an up-to-date Chrome or Edge on a computer. Other browsers may be missing the video or graphics
                features this needs; the tool tells you when that happens.
              </li>
              <li>Speed depends on your graphics chip. Processing is not real-time on most devices.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="note" id="licences" aria-labelledby="licences-title">
          <h2 id="licences-title">Models and licences</h2>
          <div class="note-body">
            <p>
              <strong>Robust Video Matting (RVM), MobileNetV3</strong> by Shanchuan Lin, Linjie Yang, Imran Saleemi and
              Soumyadip Sengupta, from the <a href={MODELS.rvm.sourceUrl}>official repository</a>. The model is licensed
              under the <a href={MODELS.rvm.licenceUrl}>GNU GPL v3.0</a>. Because this app uses it, the app’s own source code
              is also released under GPL-3.0.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>withoutBG open-weights model</strong> (version 10) by withoutBG
              (<a href={MODELS.withoutbg.sourceUrl}>source</a>, <a href="https://huggingface.co/withoutbg/withoutbg-openweights-onnx">model files</a>),
              under the <a href={MODELS.withoutbg.licenceUrl}>withoutBG open model licence</a> (Apache-2.0). It includes
              Depth Anything V2 Small (Apache-2.0) and Meta’s DINOv3 ConvNeXt, used under the
              <a href="https://ai.meta.com/resources/models-and-libraries/dinov3-license/">DINOv3 License</a>. Built with DINOv3.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>BEN2 Base</strong> by Prama LLC (<a href={MODELS.ben2.sourceUrl}>source</a>), used through the
              community <a href="https://huggingface.co/onnx-community/BEN2-ONNX">BEN2-ONNX</a> conversion, both published
              under the MIT licence. This is the public Base model, not Prama’s separate commercial model.
            </p>
            <p>
              The app also uses TensorFlow.js (Apache-2.0), Transformers.js (Apache-2.0), ONNX Runtime Web (MIT), Mediabunny
              (MPL-2.0), React (MIT), Astro (MIT) and Schibsted Grotesk (SIL Open Font Licence). Each keeps its own licence;
              see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md in the source.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </main>

    <footer class="footer">
      <p>Matte is free software under the GPL-3.0 licence. It runs entirely in your browser.</p>
    </footer>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    max-width: 1280px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--gutter) 48px;
  }

  @media (min-width: 720px) {
    .page {
      --gutter: 32px;
    }
  }

  .masthead {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 18px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .wordmark {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .masthead-note {
    color: var(--graphite);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .intro {
    display: grid;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 36px 0 28px;
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .intro {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.5fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      align-items: end;
      gap: 48px;
      padding: 52px 0 36px;
    }
  }

  .intro h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    font-weight: 680;
    letter-spacing: -0.028em;
    line-height: 1.04;
    max-width: 17ch;
  }

  .lede {
    color: var(--graphite);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.4;
    max-width: 30ch;
  }

  .studio-fallback {
    min-height: 360px;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    background: var(--stage);
    color: var(--stage-muted);
    border-radius: var(--radius-stage);
  }

  .notes {
    margin-top: 72px;
  }

  .note {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 28px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .note {
      grid-template-columns: 300px minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 32px;
    }
  }

  .note h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }

  .note-body {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .note-body ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.2em;
    display: grid;
    gap: 6px;
  }

  .footer {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding-top: 20px;
    color: var(--graphite);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }
</style>
